{
  "summary": "Optimize `CTxMemPool::GetSortedScoreWithTopology()` by replacing an `O(N log N)` `std::sort` with an `O(N)` traversal of `TxGraph`'s pre-ordered chunk index. Add `TxGraph::GetMainOrder()` to expand chunks in linearization order without comparator calls, and verify equivalence against the old sorting logic in `check()`. Also add a benchmark `RpcMempoolTxids` measuring non-verbose `getrawmempool` performance.",
  "problem": "Retrieving the global mempool transaction order requires an `O(N log N)` sort using `TxGraph::CompareMainOrder` while holding the main mempool lock `cs`. Callers of `GetSortedScoreWithTopology()`—including `getrawmempool`, P2P `mempool` dumps, and `mempool.dat` serialization—block other mempool operations longer than necessary.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description benchmarks show `RpcMempoolTxids` (10k txs) dropping from 5.10 ms to 1.07 ms and `getrawmempool false` (60k txs) dropping from 99 ms to 24 ms on a Ryzen 5 3600.",
    "PR description notes that 'time with cs held goes down in the same way, which matters for indexers that call getrawmempool every few seconds.'"
  ],
